// TEST: An arrow parameter handed a let-bound lambda whose parameter is only applied
// ============================================================================
// The value-test sibling of functions/223. `ap(f, x) = f(x)` with `x` an
// array: the passed lambda's open `v` must be an array. In 223 the lambda's
// body used `v` as a VALUE (`v * 2.0`, typed before the call), so it cannot
// be made one and stays refused. Here the body only APPLIES `v`; those
// applications were recorded while it was open and are typed as array reads
// once it is bound, so it is legal. The lambda is one body, so a second call
// passes an array again (any length: bound at its shape).
function ap(f, x) = f(x)
let g = lambda(v) -> v(0) * 2.0 + v(1)
let t = ap(g, [1.0, 2.0])
let t2 = ap(g, [5.0, 6.0, 7.0])
let i = ap(lambda(k) -> k * 3, 4)
// EXPECT: t = 4.0
// EXPECT: t2 = 16.0
// EXPECT: i = 12
